     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 3,200 mg/day for adults under medical supervision. A single 1,600 mg dose is also twice the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), which is the usual maximum for anti-inflammatory dosing.\n- **400\u2013600 mg by mouth every 6 hours** for pain or fever.\n- **1,600 mg total per day**, divided into doses such as 400 mg four times daily.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give a clinical rationale for the order note. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
